  "summary": "Bagh print is a traditional Indian handicraft originating in Bagh, Dhar district of Madhya Pradesh, India.",
  "description": "Bagh print is a traditional Indian handicraft originating in Bagh, Dhar district of Madhya Pradesh, India. The process is characterised by hand-printed wood block relief prints with naturally sourced pigments and dyes. Bagh print motifs are typically geometric, paisley, or floral compositions design, dyed with vegetable colours of red and black over a white background, and is a popular textile printing product. Its name is derived from the village Bagh located on the banks of the Bagh River.",
  "culturalContext": "Registered as a Geographical Indication of India (handicraft, Madhya Pradesh; registration 2008–09), which protects the name for products made in its place of origin by traditional methods.",
